WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.087
Industrial cyber risk does not fit neatly into traditional information-security assumptions.

00:00:06.087 --> 00:00:20.452
A loss of confidentiality may expose engineering information, but a loss of system integrity or availability can also affect machinery, product quality, safety, environmental conditions, and essential services.

00:00:20.452 --> 00:00:25.078
Security decisions must be evaluated against physical operations.

00:00:25.078 --> 00:00:35.060
OT environments combine specialized control devices, conventional computers, industrial networks, safety functions, cloud services, remote vendors, and human operators.

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:39.199
Equipment may remain in service for decades.

00:00:39.199 --> 00:00:47.234
Patching and architecture changes may require vendor support, testing, maintenance windows, and carefully planned recovery.

00:00:47.234 --> 00:00:53.807
Without a common framework, each organization or supplier may define security differently.

00:00:53.807 --> 00:01:01.355
An asset owner may request a secure system without describing risk or acceptance criteria.

00:01:01.355 --> 00:01:08.903
A supplier may describe a component as secure without explaining its capabilities or assumptions.

00:01:08.903 --> 00:01:16.937
An integrator may deliver a working process while leaving remote access and account ownership unresolved.

00:01:16.937 --> 00:01:22.050
IEC 62443 creates a common language for these conversations.

00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:30.572
It connects business and operational risk to system requirements, supplier capabilities, service responsibilities, and lifecycle practices.

00:01:30.572 --> 00:01:41.528
It encourages teams to define boundaries, identify required communication, select protection based on context, and preserve evidence that decisions were implemented.

00:01:41.528 --> 00:01:46.154
The standards also reinforce that cybersecurity is continuous.

00:01:46.154 --> 00:01:52.241
Operations change, software ages, vendors release updates, and threat conditions evolve.

00:01:52.241 --> 00:01:59.302
Security must be considered during design, procurement, integration, commissioning, operation, maintenance, and retirement.

00:01:59.302 --> 00:02:07.823
IEC 62443 exists to make that shared work more consistent, accountable, and suited to industrial reality.
